    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/en-us/filter/?job-mail-subscribe-privacy=agree&search-keyword=&work-type=faculty": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Boise State University - Search Results Skip to main content. Boise State University Home Careers How to Apply and Candidate FAQs About Boise State University Benefits Work/Life Balance Home HRS Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a strategic, collaborative Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs to serve as its Chief Academic Officer and advance academic excellence, research growth, and student success. The next Provost will help shape the future of a rapidly growing public research university through innovative, transparent, and forward-looking academic leadership. Lab Instructor - Chemistry Boise, ID September 30, 2026 Boise State University’s Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks a full-time Laboratory Instructor to teach undergraduate chemistry labs and provide student support through the Chemistry Instructional Center. This hands-on teaching role is ideal for an educator committed to engaging laboratory instruction and helping students build strong foundational chemistry skills. Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor - Respiratory Care Boise, ID, Hybrid, Remote Open until filled Boise State University’s School of Respiratory Care seeks a Clinical Assistant or Clinical Associate Professor to teach and advise students in its online, CoARC-accredited Master of Science in Respiratory Care Degree Advancement Program. This 11-month position is eligible for remote work and offers the opportunity to shape high-quality online learning while supporting student success and program excellence. Lecturer - Chemistry Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University’s Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks a full-time Lecturer to teach general chemistry and other undergraduate courses aligned with departmental needs and expertise. This teaching-focused role is ideal for an educator committed to engaging, evidence-based instruction and supporting student success in the chemical sciences. Assistant or Associate Professor - Construction Management Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University’s Department of Construction Management seeks tenure-track faculty members at the Assistant and Assistant/Associate Professor ranks to teach, conduct impactful research, and help shape the future of a rapidly growing, industry-connected program. Join a collaborative faculty community and contribute to student success, scholarship, and innovation in a department supported by strong industry partnerships and a new state-of-the-art facility. Assistant Professor - Cognitive Psychology Boise, ID September 15, 2026 Boise State University’s Department of Psychological Science seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cognitive Psychology to lead an active research program, mentor undergraduate researchers, and teach courses in cognitive psychology and related areas. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to a vibrant undergraduate-focused department while building a strong record of scholarship, teaching, and service. Chair, Department of Civil Engineering Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a collaborative and strategic leader to serve as Chair of the Department of Civil Engineering, guiding academic growth, research advancement, and industry partnerships within a rapidly evolving college and metropolitan region. This leadership role offers the opportunity to shape the future of an ABET-accredited department committed to innovation, student success, and impactful engineering education and research. Adjunct - Mathematics Boise, ID Open until filled Applications welcomed for adjunct faculty in the First Year Math Program (FYM) and Math Department. Adjunct- School of Nursing Boise, ID Open until filled Applications welcomed for expert clinical nurses to work as\nadjunct nursing faculty. Join a Talent Pool Temporary Jobs On Campus Boise State University has frequent opportunities for short-term employment, either full or part time, that often can start within a few days. Types of work can include a wide variety of specialties! Current opportunities Position Location Closes Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a strategic, collaborative Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs to serve as its Chief Academic Officer and advance academic excellence, research growth, and student success. The next Provost will help shape the future of a rapidly growing public research university through innovative, transparent, and forward-looking academic leadership. Lab Instructor - Chemistry Boise, ID September 30, 2026 Boise State University’s Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks a full-time Laboratory Instructor to teach undergraduate chemistry labs and provide student support through the Chemistry Instructional Center. This hands-on teaching role is ideal for an educator committed to engaging laboratory instruction and helping students build strong foundational chemistry skills. Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor - Respiratory Care Boise, ID, Hybrid, Remote Open until filled Boise State University’s School of Respiratory Care seeks a Clinical Assistant or Clinical Associate Professor to teach and advise students in its online, CoARC-accredited Master of Science in Respiratory Care Degree Advancement Program. This 11-month position is eligible for remote work and offers the opportunity to shape high-quality online learning while supporting student success and program excellence. Lecturer - Chemistry Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University’s Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks a full-time Lecturer to teach general chemistry and other undergraduate courses aligned with departmental needs and expertise. This teaching-focused role is ideal for an educator committed to engaging, evidence-based instruction and supporting student success in the chemical sciences. Assistant or Associate Professor - Construction Management Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University’s Department of Construction Management seeks tenure-track faculty members at the Assistant and Assistant/Associate Professor ranks to teach, conduct impactful research, and help shape the future of a rapidly growing, industry-connected program. Join a collaborative faculty community and contribute to student success, scholarship, and innovation in a department supported by strong industry partnerships and a new state-of-the-art facility. Assistant Professor - Cognitive Psychology Boise, ID September 15, 2026 Boise State University’s Department of Psychological Science seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cognitive Psychology to lead an active research program, mentor undergraduate researchers, and teach courses in cognitive psychology and related areas. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to a vibrant undergraduate-focused department while building a strong record of scholarship, teaching, and service. Chair, Department of Civil Engineering Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a collaborative and strategic leader to serve as Chair of the Department of Civil Engineering, guiding academic growth, research advancement, and industry partnerships within a rapidly evolving college and metropolitan region. This leadership role offers the opportunity to shape the future of an ABET-accredited department committed to innovation, student success, and impactful engineering education and research. Adjunct - Mathematics Boise, ID Open until filled Applications welcomed for adjunct faculty in the First Year Math Program (FYM) and Math Department. Adjunct- School of Nursing Boise, ID Open until filled Applications welcomed for expert clinical nurses to work as\nadjunct nursing faculty. Powered by PageUp Sign In Search Work Type Classified 0 Faculty 9 Non-Classified/Professional 1 Locations Boise, ID 9 Hybrid 1 Remote 1 Categories Academic Affairs 1 Adjunct Faculty 1 Administration and Business Operations 1 Athletics 0 College of Arts & Sciences 3 College of Education 0 College of Engineering 2 College of Health Sciences 1 Customer Service 0 Entry-Level 0 Event Support 0 Facilities Maintenance 0 Financial Aid 0 Graduate College 0 Health 1 Housing 0 Management 0 Marketing and Communications 0 Mechanical 0 Mid-Level 0 Research 0 Safety and Security 0 Senior-Level 1 Student Affairs & Enrollment Management 0 Student Services 0 Temporary opportunities 0 Transportation 0 Subscribe to Jobs Filter Jobs Sign In Search Work Type Classified 0 Faculty 9 Non-Classified/Professional 1 Locations Boise, ID 9 Hybrid 1 Remote 1 Categories Academic Affairs 1 Adjunct Faculty 1 Administration and Business Operations 1 Athletics 0 College of Arts & Sciences 3 College of Education 0 College of Engineering 2 College of Health Sciences 1 Customer Service 0 Entry-Level 0 Event Support 0 Facilities Maintenance 0 Financial Aid 0 Graduate College 0 Health 1 Housing 0 Management 0 Marketing and Communications 0 Mechanical 0 Mid-Level 0 Research 0 Safety and Security 0 Senior-Level 1 Student Affairs & Enrollment Management 0 Student Services 0 Temporary opportunities 0 Transportation 0 Subscribe to Jobs Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided\n                for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or \n                class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified \n                employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. \n                If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu . Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act.  The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses.  Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others.\n               You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911 ; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Accessibility Privacy Policies © 2026 \n                     All Rights Reserved. Boise State University This website stores cookies on your computer. These cookies are used to improve your website and provide more personalized services to you, both on this website and through other media. To find out more about the cookies we use, see our Privacy Policy . Close Message"
