    "https://www.boisestate.edu/jobs": {
      "title": "Boise Global Navigation",
      "description": "Boise State Careers - Boise State University Skip to main content Careers at Boise State Home Search Menu Boise Global Navigation Apply Visit Give Menu Ready to take the next step? Plan your virtual visit. Search Search All Boise State Careers at Boise State Only Boise State Careers Boise State University is a great place to make a living, make a life, and make a difference. Apply to start your meaningful career. Current Opportunities Careers at Boise State Current Opportunities Faculty Recruitment Contact HR About Boise State Human Resources Home Benefits Work/Life Balance More section menu items Join our thriving Bronco Community Boise State isn’t just any employer. We’re proud to be recognized in Forbes’ 2025 Best Employers by State list, earning a top spot in both 2024 and 2025. This marks the third consecutive Forbes honor for the university, following its recognition in 2024 as one of America’s Best Midsize Employers. We offer a competitive salary and a robust benefits plan to provide a whole-employee experience designed to enhance well-being, collaboration, innovation, and career growth. Here, you’ll join a vibrant community known for its “ blue turf thinking ” – pushing boundaries, conducting groundbreaking research, and reimagining higher education. Professional, Classified & Faculty Positions Full-time and Part-time opportunities Professional, Classified & Faculty Positions Full-time and Part-time opportunities Adjunct Faculty Part-time instructional opportunities covering a wide range of topics and disciplines. Adjunct Faculty Part-time instructional opportunities covering a wide range of topics and disciplines. Faculty Careers Join a thriving faculty community. Faculty Careers Join a thriving faculty community. Graduate Assistantships (GA) Mentored, award-based employment experiences for graduate students. Graduate Assistantships (GA) Mentored, award-based employment experiences for graduate students. Student Employment Job opportunities for current Boise State students. Student Employment Job opportunities for current Boise State students. Benefits Medical insurance, retirement plans and more. Benefits Medical insurance, retirement plans and more. Our Metropolitan Home About Boise State Boise State is located in one of the fastest growing high-tech cities in the nation and home to several corporate headquarters, state and federal offices, medical centers and media outlets. The city has garnered national recognition from U.S. News & World Report, Forbes, LinkedIn, and Inc. for being a great place to live, work and study, and has been dubbed one of the hottest cities for entrepreneurs.  With stats like these, it’s easy to see why more than 46,000 graduates have chosen to live in the Treasure Valley after earning their degree from Boise State. Our Vibrant Campus About Boise State Our Vibrant Campus About Boise State Boise and Beyond Check Out Our Metropolitan Home Boise and Beyond Check Out Our Metropolitan Home Amazing Benefits Amazing Benefits Amazing Benefits Work Life Balance Work Life Balance Work Life Balance A Day in the Life “Boise State is a place brimming with many talented people who are committed to being our best selves for students, staff and faculty. The versatility of the campus has always been impressive.” – David Weaver Senior Research Analyst, Office of Institutional Effectiveness Learn more about what it’s like working at Boise State. Video Transcript – A Day in the Life What It's Like Working At Boise State What Employees Are Saying Krishna Pakala Heather Carlson Lane Donovan Amy Vecchione David Weaver Martha Plascencia Krishna Pakala “Boise State empowers me to continue to do good work and support the mission of the university: to teach in innovative ways, research to solve complex problems and serve our community and beyond. It also renews the faith in the American Dream which is based on a set of ideals that provides opportunities to people no matter who they are or where they come from. Boise State provides me the platform to celebrate the investment my family has made in me by providing an environment to pursue my dreams. Teaching is a remarkable craft. I am very proud to be part of the education community to serve large numbers of students and it is very heartening to see such efforts are valued at Boise State.” Krishna Pakala Associate Professor, Mechanical & Biomedical Engineering Heather Carlson “I have been very fortunate to experience Boise State as a childhood fan (my parents are Boise State graduates), as a student myself, an alumna, and again as an employee. Boise State is home. When I come to work I am surrounded by individuals who care about me and treat me as part of their family. The campus — especially when classes are in session — has a buzz, a vibrancy and an energetic feeling, unlike any other place I’ve worked. Boise State, and the people who work here, are inspiring. I am honored to be a part of it.” Heather Carlson Senior Director of Marketing and Annual Giving, University Advancement Lane Donovan In my three-plus years at Boise State, I’ve managed to move up faster in my career than “I would have ever thought possible all while doing something I love—bringing high-quality education to any and all students using cutting-edge technology. The incredible team of people I get to work with on a daily basis, combined with a work-life balance that allows me time for my family and friends, is a huge reason I love being a part of the Boise State family.” Lane Donovan Multimedia Team Manager, eCampus Center Amy Vecchione, head of the Web and Emerging Technology Unit and associate professor, Albertsons Library Amy Vecchione “In my job, I get to work with a lot of units and departments across campus helping students and faculty solve problems. We create knowledge not just consume it; and in the process I love that I can foster student success and empowerment by creating a community of learning that directly impacts their success as a student and their success as they enter the workplace. I feel like I am the luckiest person on the campus to do what I do, work where I work; fostering an interdisciplinary community at Boise State University.” Amy Vecchione Assistant Director, eCampus Research and Innovation David Weaver “Boise State is a place brimming with many talented people who are committed to being our best selves for students, staff and faculty. The versatility of the campus has always been impressive.” Dr. David Weaver Senior Research Analyst, Office of Institutional Effectiveness Martha Plascencia, administrative assistant, Office of Institutional Effectiveness Martha Plascencia “Education is very important to me. Working for Boise State, I am able to further my educational goal to pursue my masters and I am able to do this due to the fee waiver benefit and the flexibility and support I receive from my leadership team. I value that flexibility to keep improving myself. Being a lifelong learner is a passion and it also helps me be able to relate to our students as I am experiencing what they are experiencing. My ultimate goal, to teach, of course!” Martha Plascencia Management Assistant, Office of Institutional Effectiveness Learn More About Applying To Boise State Applicant Resources Application FAQs Application FAQs Application FAQs Interview Process FAQs Interview Process FAQs Interview Process FAQs Notice of Intent to Hire H-1B Employees Notice of Filing Labor Condition Applications Notice of Intent to Hire H-1B Employees Notice of Filing Labor Condition Applications Careers at Boise State hr@boisestate.edu (208) 426-1616 960 S Broadway Ave., University Plaza, Ste. 100, Boise, ID 83725-1265 Secondary Navigation myBoiseState Safety, Security and Support Career Opportunities Boise State Public Radio Albertsons Library Transportation and Parking Partner with Us Morrison Center Alumni Bronco Shop and Bookstore University Administration ExtraMile Arena Broncos Logo Athletics Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on X Follow us on Youtube Follow us on LinkedIn Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy Classroom Concerns Policies Contact Boise State © 2026 All Rights Reserved\n\t\t\t\t\t\t Boise State University. Back To Top"
    },
    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/en-us/listing/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Boise State University - Recent Jobs Skip to main content. Boise State University Home Careers How to Apply and Candidate FAQs About Boise State University Benefits Work/Life Balance Home HRS Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes HVAC Technician Senior Boise, ID September 20, 2026 Facilities Operations and Maintenance supports the university’s strategic mission by professionally maintaining safe, functional and attractive facilities and grounds, while also providing quality support services to the campus community. Commercial Appliance Repair Technician Boise, ID September 20, 2026 Facilities Operations and Maintenance supports the university’s strategic mission by professionally maintaining safe, functional and attractive facilities and grounds, while also providing quality support services to the campus community. Landscape Foreman Boise, ID September 23, 2026 Facilities Operations and Maintenance supports the university’s strategic mission by professionally maintaining safe, functional, and attractive facilities and grounds, while also providing quality support services to the campus community. Building Facility Specialist Boise, ID September 23, 2026 Boise State Athletics is seeking qualified candidates to join our growing facility and event operations team. Well qualified candidates will demonstrate a high level of problem-solving ability, the ability to frequently adapt procedures and techniques to meet specialized needs. Housing and Residence Life Custodian Boise, ID September 20, 2026 Daytime shift and this position is eligible for reduced tuition on most college courses for the employee, their spouse, and their dependent child. Join a great team and perform high-level cleaning and detailing of University housing facilities prior to occupancy and provide daily custodial service for the common areas of housing facilities. This position requires regular and reliable attendance. Assistant Director, Sports Communications Boise, ID September 20, 2026 The Boise State Athletics Sports Communications office is seeking a qualified professional with a background in collegiate or professional sports communications. The ideal candidate will possess experience managing sports information for softball or volleyball programs, as well as a demonstrated ability to prepare student-athletes for media appearances and press opportunities. Administrative Assistant 2 Boise, ID September 17, 2026 The College of Education and Public Service is seeking a collaborative, service-oriented Administrative Assistant 2 to join its Education Support Team. This position provides essential administrative and operational support for education programs, faculty, staff and students, helping ensure that day-to-day work moves forward smoothly during an important period of transition for the college. The successful candidate will be organized, responsive and comfortable managing a wide range of responsibilities, including budget and financial processes, course scheduling and curriculum support, hiring and payroll transactions, travel, purchasing, records management and meeting coordination. Scholarship Specialist, Associate or Scholarship Specialist, Intermediate Boise, ID September 10, 2026 The Financial Aid & Scholarships Department is seeking a detail-oriented, student-focused Scholarship Specialist, Associate or Scholarship Specialist, Intermediate to oversee the administration, matching, and distribution of institutional, foundation, and external scholarship programs. This role serves as a key liaison between students, academic departments, donor foundations, and institutional leadership.  The primary goal of the Scholarship Specialist is to streamline the application-to-award pipeline, ensure fair access to institutional funds, and ensure compliance with federal, state, and donor regulations. Associate Director, Ticket Operations Boise, ID September 17, 2026 This position will work as part of the broader Sports & Entertainment team within the Athletics Department, and will manage concert and live entertainment ticket operations across all department facilities, including simultaneous multi-venue execution. Transportation Facilities Support Boise, ID September 16, 2026 Join Boise State’s Public Safety Team as a Transportation Facilities Support Specialist!\n\nBoise State University’s Department of Public Safety invites you to apply for the role of Transportation Facilities Support. This is more than just a maintenance role — it’s a chance to grow your skills, contribute to a collaborative team, and directly support student success.\n\nIn this hands-on role, you’ll design and fabricate signage, maintain and repair parking equipment and electronic devices, and help keep our campus clean, safe, and accessible year-round. From striping parking lots and operating snow removal equipment to maintaining shuttle stop shelters and supporting campus events, you’ll play a vital role in keeping Boise State running smoothly. Business Operations Manager Boise, ID September 13, 2026 The College of Engineering has a work environment that embraces change and provides leadership opportunities to every team member.  Reporting to the Director of the School of Computing, the Business Operations Manager position will be responsible for managing and improving all internal business operations , overseeing employee activity  and ensuring the School of Computing is on track to meet its financial goals.  Apply today to join a team of dedicated and enthusiastic professionals! Customer Service Representative 2 Boise, ID September 14, 2026 This position provides accurate and timely information, and assist students to better understand the resources they have available to pay for their education. Whether in-person, over the phone, or via email, the Customer Service Representative in this position makes a positive difference in the lives of students every day by employing outstanding customer service and effective communication skills. This role can include wearing many different hats such as that of an interviewer, a detective, a confidant, or a lifeline in order to achieve the goal of providing an experience that ensures students know they matter and belong within the Boise State community. Assistant Director, Athletic Personnel Services Boise, ID September 14, 2026 The Athletics Department is looking for a team member to join the Athletic Personnel Services (APS) Team. This position will support the department's day-to-day activities as a liaison for Human Resources, the Business Office, and the Sports & Entertainment areas by assisting with hiring, payroll, and data management of part-time support staff. Enrollment Counselor, Associate Boise, ID September 10, 2026 The Graduate Enrollment Specialist serves as the primary Graduate College contact for prospective students and supports students throughout the enrollment journey from inquiry through onboarding. This position provides admissions and enrollment guidance, coordinates enrollment communications, manages communication workflows within Slate, and supports student engagement activities designed to foster a welcoming and informed experience.\nThis position also works closely with academic programs, the Graduate Admissions Team, Extended Studies, and other campus partners to ensure prospective students receive timely information, appropriate referrals, and consistent communication throughout the inquiry, application, admission, and enrollment process. Through communication, relationship-building, and enrollment support, this position contributes to Graduate College enrollment goals and student success. Director, Facilities Boise, ID September 9, 2026 Boise State Athletics seeks applicants for the position of Director, Facilities. Under the supervision of the Assistant AD, Operations & Capital Projects, this position will be responsible for overseeing the maintenance and repairs of all building systems, including, but not limited to, HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and technical systems. This position also oversees all third-party contractors, vendor maintenance and repairs, including, but not limited to, elevators, mechanical PMs, and generator PMs. The Director, Facilities supports all Boise State Sports & Entertainment group facilities, including Albertsons Stadium, ExtraMile Arena, Dona Larsen Park, BOAS Soccer and Tennis Complex, and associated practice, competitive, office, team, and event spaces. Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a strategic, collaborative Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs to serve as its Chief Academic Officer and advance academic excellence, research growth, and student success. The next Provost will help shape the future of a rapidly growing public research university through innovative, transparent, and forward-looking academic leadership. Internship Program Data and Operations Specialist Boise, ID September 13, 2026 Career Services at Boise State University is seeking a collaborative and forward-thinking Internship Program Data and Operations Specialist to drive Boise State's Internship Program forward through student mentoring, faculty support, and employer engagement. This role partners with campus and employer stakeholders to connect students with internships that enhance career readiness and post-graduate success. The ideal candidate is student-centered and committed to developing new ways to connect students to internships across a wide range of academic departments. Deputy Director of Event Security Operations Boise, ID September 13, 2026 Step into a high-impact leadership role overseeing security for Boise State’s largest and most complex events—including major stadium operations.\n\nAs Deputy Director, you’ll lead the university’s event security program, guiding strategy, staffing, and operations across all venues. You’ll oversee a team of leaders, shape policy, manage budgets, and ensure readiness for high-risk, high-attendance events.\n\nThis role is at the center of it all—partnering with Athletics, campus leadership, and law enforcement to deliver safe, well-coordinated events. You’ll play a key role in incident command, large-scale planning, and continuous program improvement.\n\nIf you bring strong leadership, event security expertise, and the ability to make sound decisions in dynamic environments, this is your opportunity to lead at scale. Lab Instructor - Chemistry Boise, ID September 30, 2026 Boise State University’s Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks a full-time Laboratory Instructor to teach undergraduate chemistry labs and provide student support through the Chemistry Instructional Center. This hands-on teaching role is ideal for an educator committed to engaging laboratory instruction and helping students build strong foundational chemistry skills. Lecturer - Chemistry Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University’s Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks a full-time Lecturer to teach general chemistry and other undergraduate courses aligned with departmental needs and expertise. This teaching-focused role is ideal for an educator committed to engaging, evidence-based instruction and supporting student success in the chemical sciences. Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor - Respiratory Care Boise, ID, Hybrid, Remote Open until filled Boise State University’s School of Respiratory Care seeks a Clinical Assistant or Clinical Associate Professor to teach and advise students in its online, CoARC-accredited Master of Science in Respiratory Care Degree Advancement Program. This 11-month position is eligible for remote work and offers the opportunity to shape high-quality online learning while supporting student success and program excellence. Post Doctoral Research Fellow Boise, ID Open until filled The Department of Geosciences at Boise State University invites applications for a full-time Post Doctoral Research Fellow to calibrate rare-earth element (REE)–based thermodynamically-valid thermobarometers for rock-forming minerals relevant to igneous and metamorphic processes. The Post Doctoral Research Fellow will work collaboratively with Professor Matthew J. Kohn and his research group. This work is funded for two years by a grant from the National Science Foundation (EAR 2547559). Major responsibilities are to focus on REE partitioning between garnet and clinopyroxene, potentially expanding consideration to other minerals. Additional responsibilities include semi-annual outreach to local educational institutions and help developing online teaching videos in thermodynamics and petrology. Vice President of Finance and Chief Financial Officer (VP-CFO) Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a Vice President for Finance and Chief Financial Officer (VP-CFO) to provide strategic leadership over the university’s financial operations, ensuring fiscal integrity, sustainability, and alignment with institutional priorities. This executive role partners closely with campus leadership to support growth, innovation, and student success through sound financial stewardship and forward-looking planning. Assistant or Associate Professor - Construction Management Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University’s Department of Construction Management seeks tenure-track faculty members at the Assistant and Assistant/Associate Professor ranks to teach, conduct impactful research, and help shape the future of a rapidly growing, industry-connected program. Join a collaborative faculty community and contribute to student success, scholarship, and innovation in a department supported by strong industry partnerships and a new state-of-the-art facility. Assistant Professor - Cognitive Psychology Boise, ID September 15, 2026 Boise State University’s Department of Psychological Science seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cognitive Psychology to lead an active research program, mentor undergraduate researchers, and teach courses in cognitive psychology and related areas. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to a vibrant undergraduate-focused department while building a strong record of scholarship, teaching, and service. Chair, Department of Civil Engineering Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a collaborative and strategic leader to serve as Chair of the Department of Civil Engineering, guiding academic growth, research advancement, and industry partnerships within a rapidly evolving college and metropolitan region. This leadership role offers the opportunity to shape the future of an ABET-accredited department committed to innovation, student success, and impactful engineering education and research. Adjunct - Mathematics Boise, ID Open until filled Applications welcomed for adjunct faculty in the First Year Math Program (FYM) and Math Department. Adjunct- School of Nursing Boise, ID Open until filled Applications welcomed for expert clinical nurses to work as\nadjunct nursing faculty. Join a Talent Pool Temporary Jobs On Campus Boise State University has frequent opportunities for short-term employment, either full or part time, that often can start within a few days. Types of work can include a wide variety of specialties! Current opportunities Position Location Closes HVAC Technician Senior Boise, ID September 20, 2026 Facilities Operations and Maintenance supports the university’s strategic mission by professionally maintaining safe, functional and attractive facilities and grounds, while also providing quality support services to the campus community. Commercial Appliance Repair Technician Boise, ID September 20, 2026 Facilities Operations and Maintenance supports the university’s strategic mission by professionally maintaining safe, functional and attractive facilities and grounds, while also providing quality support services to the campus community. Landscape Foreman Boise, ID September 23, 2026 Facilities Operations and Maintenance supports the university’s strategic mission by professionally maintaining safe, functional, and attractive facilities and grounds, while also providing quality support services to the campus community. Building Facility Specialist Boise, ID September 23, 2026 Boise State Athletics is seeking qualified candidates to join our growing facility and event operations team. Well qualified candidates will demonstrate a high level of problem-solving ability, the ability to frequently adapt procedures and techniques to meet specialized needs. Housing and Residence Life Custodian Boise, ID September 20, 2026 Daytime shift and this position is eligible for reduced tuition on most college courses for the employee, their spouse, and their dependent child. Join a great team and perform high-level cleaning and detailing of University housing facilities prior to occupancy and provide daily custodial service for the common areas of housing facilities. This position requires regular and reliable attendance. Assistant Director, Sports Communications Boise, ID September 20, 2026 The Boise State Athletics Sports Communications office is seeking a qualified professional with a background in collegiate or professional sports communications. The ideal candidate will possess experience managing sports information for softball or volleyball programs, as well as a demonstrated ability to prepare student-athletes for media appearances and press opportunities. Administrative Assistant 2 Boise, ID September 17, 2026 The College of Education and Public Service is seeking a collaborative, service-oriented Administrative Assistant 2 to join its Education Support Team. This position provides essential administrative and operational support for education programs, faculty, staff and students, helping ensure that day-to-day work moves forward smoothly during an important period of transition for the college. The successful candidate will be organized, responsive and comfortable managing a wide range of responsibilities, including budget and financial processes, course scheduling and curriculum support, hiring and payroll transactions, travel, purchasing, records management and meeting coordination. Scholarship Specialist, Associate or Scholarship Specialist, Intermediate Boise, ID September 10, 2026 The Financial Aid & Scholarships Department is seeking a detail-oriented, student-focused Scholarship Specialist, Associate or Scholarship Specialist, Intermediate to oversee the administration, matching, and distribution of institutional, foundation, and external scholarship programs. This role serves as a key liaison between students, academic departments, donor foundations, and institutional leadership.  The primary goal of the Scholarship Specialist is to streamline the application-to-award pipeline, ensure fair access to institutional funds, and ensure compliance with federal, state, and donor regulations. Associate Director, Ticket Operations Boise, ID September 17, 2026 This position will work as part of the broader Sports & Entertainment team within the Athletics Department, and will manage concert and live entertainment ticket operations across all department facilities, including simultaneous multi-venue execution. Transportation Facilities Support Boise, ID September 16, 2026 Join Boise State’s Public Safety Team as a Transportation Facilities Support Specialist!\n\nBoise State University’s Department of Public Safety invites you to apply for the role of Transportation Facilities Support. This is more than just a maintenance role — it’s a chance to grow your skills, contribute to a collaborative team, and directly support student success.\n\nIn this hands-on role, you’ll design and fabricate signage, maintain and repair parking equipment and electronic devices, and help keep our campus clean, safe, and accessible year-round. From striping parking lots and operating snow removal equipment to maintaining shuttle stop shelters and supporting campus events, you’ll play a vital role in keeping Boise State running smoothly. Business Operations Manager Boise, ID September 13, 2026 The College of Engineering has a work environment that embraces change and provides leadership opportunities to every team member.  Reporting to the Director of the School of Computing, the Business Operations Manager position will be responsible for managing and improving all internal business operations , overseeing employee activity  and ensuring the School of Computing is on track to meet its financial goals.  Apply today to join a team of dedicated and enthusiastic professionals! Customer Service Representative 2 Boise, ID September 14, 2026 This position provides accurate and timely information, and assist students to better understand the resources they have available to pay for their education. Whether in-person, over the phone, or via email, the Customer Service Representative in this position makes a positive difference in the lives of students every day by employing outstanding customer service and effective communication skills. This role can include wearing many different hats such as that of an interviewer, a detective, a confidant, or a lifeline in order to achieve the goal of providing an experience that ensures students know they matter and belong within the Boise State community. Assistant Director, Athletic Personnel Services Boise, ID September 14, 2026 The Athletics Department is looking for a team member to join the Athletic Personnel Services (APS) Team. This position will support the department's day-to-day activities as a liaison for Human Resources, the Business Office, and the Sports & Entertainment areas by assisting with hiring, payroll, and data management of part-time support staff. Enrollment Counselor, Associate Boise, ID September 10, 2026 The Graduate Enrollment Specialist serves as the primary Graduate College contact for prospective students and supports students throughout the enrollment journey from inquiry through onboarding. This position provides admissions and enrollment guidance, coordinates enrollment communications, manages communication workflows within Slate, and supports student engagement activities designed to foster a welcoming and informed experience.\nThis position also works closely with academic programs, the Graduate Admissions Team, Extended Studies, and other campus partners to ensure prospective students receive timely information, appropriate referrals, and consistent communication throughout the inquiry, application, admission, and enrollment process. Through communication, relationship-building, and enrollment support, this position contributes to Graduate College enrollment goals and student success. Director, Facilities Boise, ID September 9, 2026 Boise State Athletics seeks applicants for the position of Director, Facilities. Under the supervision of the Assistant AD, Operations & Capital Projects, this position will be responsible for overseeing the maintenance and repairs of all building systems, including, but not limited to, HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and technical systems. This position also oversees all third-party contractors, vendor maintenance and repairs, including, but not limited to, elevators, mechanical PMs, and generator PMs. The Director, Facilities supports all Boise State Sports & Entertainment group facilities, including Albertsons Stadium, ExtraMile Arena, Dona Larsen Park, BOAS Soccer and Tennis Complex, and associated practice, competitive, office, team, and event spaces. Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a strategic, collaborative Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs to serve as its Chief Academic Officer and advance academic excellence, research growth, and student success. The next Provost will help shape the future of a rapidly growing public research university through innovative, transparent, and forward-looking academic leadership. Internship Program Data and Operations Specialist Boise, ID September 13, 2026 Career Services at Boise State University is seeking a collaborative and forward-thinking Internship Program Data and Operations Specialist to drive Boise State's Internship Program forward through student mentoring, faculty support, and employer engagement. This role partners with campus and employer stakeholders to connect students with internships that enhance career readiness and post-graduate success. The ideal candidate is student-centered and committed to developing new ways to connect students to internships across a wide range of academic departments. Deputy Director of Event Security Operations Boise, ID September 13, 2026 Step into a high-impact leadership role overseeing security for Boise State’s largest and most complex events—including major stadium operations.\n\nAs Deputy Director, you’ll lead the university’s event security program, guiding strategy, staffing, and operations across all venues. You’ll oversee a team of leaders, shape policy, manage budgets, and ensure readiness for high-risk, high-attendance events.\n\nThis role is at the center of it all—partnering with Athletics, campus leadership, and law enforcement to deliver safe, well-coordinated events. You’ll play a key role in incident command, large-scale planning, and continuous program improvement.\n\nIf you bring strong leadership, event security expertise, and the ability to make sound decisions in dynamic environments, this is your opportunity to lead at scale. Lab Instructor - Chemistry Boise, ID September 30, 2026 Boise State University’s Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks a full-time Laboratory Instructor to teach undergraduate chemistry labs and provide student support through the Chemistry Instructional Center. This hands-on teaching role is ideal for an educator committed to engaging laboratory instruction and helping students build strong foundational chemistry skills. Lecturer - Chemistry Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University’s Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks a full-time Lecturer to teach general chemistry and other undergraduate courses aligned with departmental needs and expertise. This teaching-focused role is ideal for an educator committed to engaging, evidence-based instruction and supporting student success in the chemical sciences. Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor - Respiratory Care Boise, ID, Hybrid, Remote Open until filled Boise State University’s School of Respiratory Care seeks a Clinical Assistant or Clinical Associate Professor to teach and advise students in its online, CoARC-accredited Master of Science in Respiratory Care Degree Advancement Program. This 11-month position is eligible for remote work and offers the opportunity to shape high-quality online learning while supporting student success and program excellence. Post Doctoral Research Fellow Boise, ID Open until filled The Department of Geosciences at Boise State University invites applications for a full-time Post Doctoral Research Fellow to calibrate rare-earth element (REE)–based thermodynamically-valid thermobarometers for rock-forming minerals relevant to igneous and metamorphic processes. The Post Doctoral Research Fellow will work collaboratively with Professor Matthew J. Kohn and his research group. This work is funded for two years by a grant from the National Science Foundation (EAR 2547559). Major responsibilities are to focus on REE partitioning between garnet and clinopyroxene, potentially expanding consideration to other minerals. Additional responsibilities include semi-annual outreach to local educational institutions and help developing online teaching videos in thermodynamics and petrology. Vice President of Finance and Chief Financial Officer (VP-CFO) Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a Vice President for Finance and Chief Financial Officer (VP-CFO) to provide strategic leadership over the university’s financial operations, ensuring fiscal integrity, sustainability, and alignment with institutional priorities. This executive role partners closely with campus leadership to support growth, innovation, and student success through sound financial stewardship and forward-looking planning. Assistant or Associate Professor - Construction Management Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University’s Department of Construction Management seeks tenure-track faculty members at the Assistant and Assistant/Associate Professor ranks to teach, conduct impactful research, and help shape the future of a rapidly growing, industry-connected program. Join a collaborative faculty community and contribute to student success, scholarship, and innovation in a department supported by strong industry partnerships and a new state-of-the-art facility. Assistant Professor - Cognitive Psychology Boise, ID September 15, 2026 Boise State University’s Department of Psychological Science seeks a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cognitive Psychology to lead an active research program, mentor undergraduate researchers, and teach courses in cognitive psychology and related areas. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to a vibrant undergraduate-focused department while building a strong record of scholarship, teaching, and service. Chair, Department of Civil Engineering Boise, ID Open until filled Boise State University seeks a collaborative and strategic leader to serve as Chair of the Department of Civil Engineering, guiding academic growth, research advancement, and industry partnerships within a rapidly evolving college and metropolitan region. This leadership role offers the opportunity to shape the future of an ABET-accredited department committed to innovation, student success, and impactful engineering education and research. Adjunct - Mathematics Boise, ID Open until filled Applications welcomed for adjunct faculty in the First Year Math Program (FYM) and Math Department. Adjunct- School of Nursing Boise, ID Open until filled Applications welcomed for expert clinical nurses to work as\nadjunct nursing faculty. Powered by PageUp Sign In Search Work Type Classified 8 Faculty 9 Non-Classified/Professional 12 Locations Boise, ID 28 Hybrid 1 Remote 1 Categories Academic Affairs 1 Adjunct Faculty 1 Administration and Business Operations 5 Athletics 5 College of Arts & Sciences 4 College of Education 1 College of Engineering 3 College of Health Sciences 1 Customer Service 1 Entry-Level 7 Event Support 2 Facilities Maintenance 6 Financial Aid 2 Graduate College 1 Health 1 Housing 1 Management 1 Marketing and Communications 1 Mechanical 2 Mid-Level 5 Research 2 Safety and Security 2 Senior-Level 6 Student Affairs & Enrollment Management 3 Student Services 1 Temporary opportunities 1 Transportation 1 Subscribe to Jobs Filter Jobs Sign In Search Work Type Classified 8 Faculty 9 Non-Classified/Professional 12 Locations Boise, ID 28 Hybrid 1 Remote 1 Categories Academic Affairs 1 Adjunct Faculty 1 Administration and Business Operations 5 Athletics 5 College of Arts & Sciences 4 College of Education 1 College of Engineering 3 College of Health Sciences 1 Customer Service 1 Entry-Level 7 Event Support 2 Facilities Maintenance 6 Financial Aid 2 Graduate College 1 Health 1 Housing 1 Management 1 Marketing and Communications 1 Mechanical 2 Mid-Level 5 Research 2 Safety and Security 2 Senior-Level 6 Student Affairs & Enrollment Management 3 Student Services 1 Temporary opportunities 1 Transportation 1 Subscribe to Jobs Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided\n                for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or \n                class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified \n                employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. \n                If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu . Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act.  The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses.  Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others.\n               You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911 ; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Accessibility Privacy Policies © 2026 \n                     All Rights Reserved. Boise State University This website stores cookies on your computer. These cookies are used to improve your website and provide more personalized services to you, both on this website and through other media. To find out more about the cookies we use, see our Privacy Policy . Close Message"
